  "body": "The dev `post` binary writes a program before it handles the post's warnings, so it can write `F0.` and then report the warning.\n\n## Evidence\n\n`assets/posts/haas.cps:136-137`: the below-step positive feed calls `msg(...)` and then still returns `pt(s)`, which is `F0.`.\n\nEvery in-app path blocks on warnings (`posting.rs:717`, `posting_mounts.rs:348`, `posting_per_op.rs:240`), so a user never gets `F0.`. The dev `post` binary writes `out.program` (`bin/post.rs:206`) before it handles warnings (`:210`), so that tool writes `F0.` plus the warning.\n\nThe decision record's \"never posted as F0.\" holds for the app, not for that dev tool. The pin checks the message, not the absence of `F0.`.\n\n## What to do\n\nMake the dev `post` binary handle warnings before it writes the program, or make the below-step path return no feed word. Then the tool cannot write `F0.`.\n\n## Related\n\n- #3689: the Haas feed-decimal change and its review.\n",
